From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dtl: make the trivial-mode mutator non-const

GCC 14 rejects enableTrivial() because the method is const but assigns to the
non-mutable trivial member. The method has no callers in tora 3.2, and the
matching enable/disable methods are mutators, so remove the incorrect const
qualifier instead of weakening the member's const semantics.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of bundled dtl Diff.hpp
Patch-License: BSD-3-Clause
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Applies-To: tora 3.2 bundled dtl
Remove-When: the bundled dtl no longer declares enableTrivial() as const
---
 extlibs/dtl/dtl/Diff.hpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extlibs/dtl/dtl/Diff.hpp b/extlibs/dtl/dtl/Diff.hpp
--- a/extlibs/dtl/dtl/Diff.hpp
+++ b/extlibs/dtl/dtl/Diff.hpp
@@ -161,11 +161,11 @@ namespace dtl {
         bool trivialEnabled () const {
             return trivial;
         }
         
-        void enableTrivial () const {
+        void enableTrivial () {
             this->trivial = true;
         }
         
         void disableTrivial () {
             this->trivial = false;
         }
-- 
